course: dictionary
lesson: 2239
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Look at the words around the word, because they are its clues. «Crab» can name an animal, a food, or a grumpy person.
explain: «Wild hermit crabs sometimes queue by size and swap shells, one after another.» Here crab means an animal, because you can picture it moving into a shell on a beach. Ask yourself which meaning fits, then put it into the sentence to check.
explain: «Dad ordered crab for dinner, with lemon and bread.» Words like dinner and ordered show that crab is the meat you eat. Ellie says, «Mum is being crabby today», and crabby shows the informal meaning: grumpy.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A crab is a sea or shore animal with a hard shell, eight legs and two big claws, which is often called pincers.
fact: Crab can also mean the meat of this animal, eaten as food.
fact: Informally, a crab is a grumpy person, and «crabby» means grumpy.
fact: Crabs often walk sideways, and many can grow back a lost claw.
exercise: «Crabs raise their claws to look bigger.» In this sentence, what is a crab? | A type of boat | A kind of cake | A grumpy person | *An animal with a hard shell and two claws
exercise: Ellie says, «Mum is being crabby today.» What does crabby mean? | Covered in sand | Hungry for seafood | Happy and singing | *Grumpy
exercise: «Dad ordered crab for dinner, with lemon and bread.» What is crab here? | A grumpy waiter | A rock pool | *The meat of the animal, eaten as food | An animal in the sea
test: «Wild hermit crabs sometimes queue by size and swap shells.» Which meaning of crab fits? | A kind of seaweed | The meat eaten at dinner | A grumpy person | *An animal with a hard shell
test: Ruby reads, «Walk like a crab, sideways across the sand.» What does this tell you? | Crab always means dinner | *Crabs often walk sideways | Crabs walk backwards | Crabs can fly
exam: In «She was a crab all morning, so we let her be», what does crab mean and which clue shows it? | An animal, because she was on the beach | A piece of seafood, because we had lunch | A shell, because it was hard | *A grumpy person, because we let her be all morning
